MEMORY NOW
LESSONS (9 of 12 slots):
[L2] Universal triage: use literal timestamps from the page header (now() returns nothing). 3 parallel queries: alerts, deployments, config_changes over last ~36-40h, all services. Then one hourly CASE-pivot of p95/error_rate/request_count/cpu for the ALERTING service over 32h (compare same hour prior day); logs by service/level/code only if needed. <=5 queries settled p-002..p-023. (evidence: p-002, p-005, p-008, p-012, p-016, p-018, p-020, p-021, p-023)
[L4] Caching/serving-path deploys (e.g. inventory-service/v8.0.4 stale-while-revalidate, day 3) reset metric baselines. After such a deploy compare to post-deploy hours, not remembered numbers, and treat a sustained p95/error_rate shift starting at deploy time as real. Post-v8.0.4 inventory settled at 83-96ms and stayed there through day 6. Status: baseline confirmed stable p-008. (evidence: p-002, p-003, p-004, p-008)
[L5] Critical checkout_error_rate_high: pivot pool_utilization/wait_ms, error_rate, dependency_latency_ms, payments_db_cpu for checkout-api AND payment-orchestrator. Pool 0.24->0.97, wait 15->4000ms, err 0.005->0.16, dependency flat ~330ms, no changed vendor = pool exhaustion. Split: db_cpu flat -> max_connections cut (L6); db_cpu 0.3->0.85 -> bad deploy (L11). (evidence: p-005, p-028, p-031)
[L6] Repeat offender: actor cost-optimizer cuts payments.max_connections 100->20 at 09:00 UTC (d4, d22); breakage shows only at ~19:00 UTC peak, so late onset does NOT clear a config change. Decoys (cosmetic deploys near a page; check changed_components): checkout v4.22.0 banner, v4.23.0 help-link (d28), order v2.3.4 footnote, v2.4.0 packing-slip, inventory v8.1.0 sku-label, search v5.6.2 typo. (evidence: p-005, p-011, p-016, p-020, p-023, p-028, p-034, p-037)
[L7] Pool-exhaustion fix pattern: restoring payments.max_connections 20->100 isn't enough - pods keep stale pools, so a recycle_pods action follows minutes later (d4; d22 restore 19:25 UTC, recycle 19:27, alert resolved 19:28). If a later page fires after that restore+recycle pair, the checkout incident is already closed - don't re-litigate it; investigate only the alerting service. Confirmed d22. (evidence: p-005, p-028, p-029)
[L8] Paired critical checkout_error_rate_high + payrail_upstream_timeout: check dependency_latency_ms for checkout-api AND payment-orchestrator. If it jumps ~325ms -> ~8000ms with error_rate ~0.005 -> ~0.2 on BOTH, and connection_pool_utilization stays at baseline (~0.25/0.24), it's external, not pool exhaustion. Confirm with vendor_snapshots changed=True; resolve with that snapshot id. Worked p-011. (evidence: p-011)
[L9] Query gotchas: SELECTing vendor_snapshots.published_at fails (needs pytz) - omit it; "first"/"last" reserved as aliases. Vendor outages: WHERE event_time>=T AND (changed=True OR current_status<>'operational') - unfiltered floods operational noise. Log level values are UPPERCASE (ERROR/INFO); filtering level IN ('error','warn') returns nothing. Metrics can be per-minute, not only 15-min. (evidence: p-011, p-031)
[L10] Self-resolving latency warnings rotate on a 4-day cycle: inventory d14/18/22/26/30, notif d15/19/23/27, order d16/20/24/28, search d17/21/25/29. Always 22:10 UTC, resolves ~22:35. Such days often have ZERO deploys/configs in 40h. Any solo *_latency_high: 3 queries (alerts/deploys/configs) + hourly p95/err/req vs prior day; no same-svc change -> dismiss. (d30 confirmed) (evidence: p-012, p-021, p-024, p-027, p-030, p-032, p-033, p-034, p-035, p-036, p-037, p-038, p-039)
[L12] Pool exhaustion can be deploy-caused: d24 payment-orchestrator v9.4.2 18:35 UTC (changed_components=payment-enrichment-query) saturated payments DB (db_cpu 0.3->0.85) ~25min later; checkout err 0.16, payment_success 0.995->0.84. Clincher: logs QUERY_SLOW "Enrichment query >4000ms" + CONNECTION_POOL_TIMEOUT. Fix = rollback deploy (v9.4.1, 19:22 UTC). Decoy: checkout log_level->debug 17:05 UTC. (evidence: p-031)
KNOWN NOISE (1 of 3 slots):
